    "upskill.level1.title": "Getting Started",
    "upskill.level1.desc": "The basics — your first photo, your first description, your first sale.",
    "upskill.level2.title": "Going Digital",
    "upskill.level2.desc": "Catalogues, social media, and talking to customers online.",
    "upskill.level3.title": "Growing Your Craft Business",
    "upskill.level3.desc": "Branding, marketing, pricing, and building a real online presence.",
    "upskill.module.catalogues.title": "Building a digital catalogue",
    "upskill.module.catalogues.body": "Your catalogue is often the first thing a serious buyer sees. Keep it simple: your best photos, clear pricing, and a short line about each product's material and technique. Update it whenever you add new work.",
    "upskill.module.social.title": "Social media content that works",
    "upskill.module.social.body": "Post consistently rather than perfectly. A photo with one honest sentence about the piece usually does better than an over-produced post. Use Promote to draft captions, then add your own voice before posting.",
    "upskill.module.presentation.title": "Presenting your product well",
    "upskill.module.presentation.body": "Plain background, good light, and a straight-on angle beat a cluttered, artistic shot almost every time online. Show scale with a hand or a common object next to the piece so buyers understand the real size.",
    "upskill.module.communication.title": "Talking to customers online",
    "upskill.module.communication.body": "Reply promptly, be clear about price and delivery time upfront, and don't be afraid to explain why handmade work costs what it does. Most lost sales come from silence, not from price objections.",
    "upskill.module.branding.title": "Building a simple brand",
    "upskill.module.branding.body": "You don't need a logo to have a brand — consistency does the work. Use the same name, the same photo style, and the same tone every time you post, so people recognize your work before they even read your name.",
    "upskill.module.marketing.title": "Digital marketing basics",
    "upskill.module.marketing.body": "Start with the one channel your actual customers already use — usually WhatsApp or Instagram for most artisans — instead of trying to be everywhere at once. Depth on one platform beats a thin presence on five.",
    "upskill.module.pricingAdvanced.title": "Pricing with confidence",
    "upskill.module.pricingAdvanced.body": "Always price in your labour time, not just material cost — this is the single most common mistake. Use the Calculator to work out a fair price, and hold that price; discounting every time someone asks trains customers to always ask.",
    "upskill.module.selling.title": "Selling online",
    "upskill.module.selling.body": "Whether you're selling through WhatsApp, Instagram, or a marketplace, the fundamentals are the same: clear photos, honest descriptions, a fair price, and a fast reply. Master those before worrying about which platform to add next.",
    "upskill.module.presence.title": "Building a lasting online presence",
    "upskill.module.presence.body": "A public {{BRAND}} page, a consistent posting habit, and real customer reviews compound over time into something a single good post never will. Think in months, not days.",
